# CAT1a: If a signal supporting a physiological alarm is of insufficient
# quality, the alarm is flagged as likely false positive.
#
# ?alarm is pre-bound by assess.py (the arriving alarm being evaluated).
# Walks ?alarm's OWN technical pathway (device -> functional unit -> sensor
# -> signal -> analysis -> metric, all BACKGROUND facts asserted by
# ground_chain — see op_knowledge.py) and asks whether that exact Signal
# particular currently carries a non-Good hasQualityState. That fact is
# CONDITION, so it is present in the query graph only while the alarm that
# reported it is active or (per mda:persistsPostAlarm) within its post-alarm
# window — assess.py builds the query graph at ?alarm's own arrival instant,
# so a fault reported by ?alarm itself would also match; in practice a
# physiological archetype's own blueprint does not carry hasQualityState, so
# this only fires from a DIFFERENT, still-active/persisting alarm on the
# same pathway. See EVALUATION/CQs/temporal/CQ9_technical_invalidity.rq for
# the coincidence-based precursor to this rule (same structural proxy, but
# matched per-tick rather than per-arriving-alarm).
#
# Requires ?alarm's message -> functional-unit edge (mda:triggeredBy), which
# op_knowledge.py's grounding never asserts on the operational graph
# (confirmed: only the static blueprint catalogue, kg_generated.ttl, carries
# it, and there via Device, not directly — see EVALUATION/CQs/
# post_enrichment/CQ2_shared_sensing_pathway.rq's use of that longer path
# against that file). assess.py's add_triggered_by adds the edge back in,
# targeting the arriving alarm's OWN FunctionalUnit particular directly
# (skipping the Device hop CQ2 needs) — see its docstring for why going
# through Device instead is actively wrong operationally, not just longer.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX qualitystate: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/quality-state/>

SELECT ?signal ?quality WHERE {
  ?alarm mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy/mda:hasSensor ?sensor .
  ?sensor mda:sensorProducesSignal ?signal .
  ?signal mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric ?metric .
  ?signal mda:hasQualityState ?quality .
  FILTER(?quality != qualitystate:Good)
}
